## Part 2 — Source code: MIT Licence

This covers the following paths **only**, once they exist:

`src/` · `tests/` · `migrations/` · `web/` · `panel/` · `Makefile` · `pyproject.toml` ·
`alembic.ini` · `.pre-commit-config.yaml`

It does **not** cover any creative content those paths may read, generate, embed or display.

> At the time of writing, none of these paths contains code — the project is at the content stage.
> This part is stated in advance so the boundary is settled before code exists, and may be changed
> to Apache-2.0 (the alternative named in C10) at any time before the first code is committed.

